      "post_subject": "PGF-01 exposure",
      "content_md": "8) Just a quick question to confirm. I opened my box of holographic plates in the darkest, darkest of dark places I could find. No noticable light after two minutes of letting my eyes adjust. After finally figuring out that there were two small levers, each one on opposite sides of the box (it's funny how I fumbled around. You had to be there) I got one plate out to have a reaistic idea for composition of the subject.\n\nAnyway, after exposing the test plate to white light the glass still appears transparent with a slight tinge. I was under the impression exposure would make it darker. Is that wrong?",
